From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: File Explorer's navigations show the new folder only once it is drawn as the prototype's

shell32's CreateViewWindow shows the new view and updates it (and its WM_SHOWWINDOW updates the list) inside
ExplorerBrowser's navigation, before the browser reports the view or the navigation as complete, which is when
PS5_Proton's File Explorer (pw_shell_explorer.h) gives the list its columns, rows and drawing. So every folder to folder
navigation first painted Wine's classic list, then the prototype's (the owner saw it on the console). The browser's
events tell pw_shell_explorer.h when a navigation starts, when its view is created and when it fails: from the start
the browser's window does not draw, so the old folder stays on screen until the new view is styled and drawn.
---
--- a/programs/explorer/explorer.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/explorer.c
@@ -311,16 +311,22 @@
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI IExplorerBrowserEventsImpl_fnOnNavigationFailed(IExplorerBrowserEvents *iface, PCIDLIST_ABSOLUTE pidl)
 {
+    IExplorerBrowserEventsImpl *This = impl_from_IExplorerBrowserEvents(iface);
+    if (This->info->mihawk) pw_explorer_navigation_failed(This->info);
     return S_OK;
 }
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI IExplorerBrowserEventsImpl_fnOnNavigationPending(IExplorerBrowserEvents *iface, PCIDLIST_ABSOLUTE pidl)
 {
+    IExplorerBrowserEventsImpl *This = impl_from_IExplorerBrowserEvents(iface);
+    if (This->info->mihawk) pw_explorer_navigation_pending(This->info);
     return S_OK;
 }
 
 static HRESULT WINAPI IExplorerBrowserEventsImpl_fnOnViewCreated(IExplorerBrowserEvents *iface, IShellView *psv)
 {
+    IExplorerBrowserEventsImpl *This = impl_from_IExplorerBrowserEvents(iface);
+    if (This->info->mihawk) pw_explorer_view_created(This->info, psv);
     return S_OK;
 }
 
